  "notes": "Refers to a temporary or permanent halt in fighting between opposing forces. Unlike {終戦|しゅうせん} (end of war), {停戦|ていせん} implies a pause that may or may not lead to permanent peace.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {停戦|ていせん}{協定|きょうてい}: ceasefire agreement\n- {停戦|ていせん}{交渉|こうしょう}: ceasefire negotiations\n- {停戦|ていせん}{合意|ごうい}: ceasefire accord\n- {即時|そくじ}{停戦|ていせん}: immediate ceasefire\n- {停戦|ていせん}ライン: ceasefire line\n- {停戦|ていせん}{違反|いはん}: ceasefire violation\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {休戦|きゅうせん}: armistice — slightly more formal, often used for longer-term truces\n- {終戦|しゅうせん}: end of war — refers to the final conclusion of hostilities, not a temporary halt\n- {講和|こうわ}: peace — refers to formal peace negotiations or treaties after conflict ends",
